<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Cologne</h1><p class="st-meta">460 CE – 509 CE (approx.) · capital Cologne</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Kingdom of the Rhineland Franks at Cologne, absorbed by Clovis through murder around 509.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/franks">Franks</a> of the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, later called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ripuarian-franks">Ripuarian Franks</a>, took over <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-cologne">Cologne</a> in the mid 5th century as Roman power collapsed. By the late 5th century they had their own king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigibert-the-lame">Sigibert</a>, who ruled from the former Roman capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germania-inferior">Germania Inferior</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigibert-the-lame">Sigibert</a>, called the Lame from a wound received fighting the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/alemanni">Alemanni</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulpich">Zülpich</a>, was an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis</a> and sent his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chloderic">Chloderic</a> to fight the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vouille">Vouillé</a> in 507. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ripuarian-franks">Ripuarian Franks</a> kept their own law, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lex-ripuaria">Lex Ripuaria</a>, written down in the 7th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregory-of-tours">Gregory of Tours</a> relates that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis</a> incited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chloderic">Chloderic</a> to murder his father, then had Chloderic killed and was raised on a shield as king by the people of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-cologne">Cologne</a>, around 509. The realm became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-franks">Kingdom of the Franks</a> and later of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/austrasia">Austrasia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 460 CE – 509 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:68.86%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>460 CE – 509 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cologne</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sigibert the Lame, Chloderic</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Germanic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Frankish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ripuarian Franks, Rhineland Franks</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=484&amp;focus=kingdom-of-cologne" aria-label="Kingdom of Cologne on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4838 411 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Cologne lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5158 667L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5158 667h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5158 667h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cologne. <a href="/atlas?year=484&amp;focus=kingdom-of-cologne">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

